.TH MAILER.PY 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
mailer.py \- send a digest or an escalation through Microsoft Graph, behind the recipient allowlist
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mailer.py
.BI \-\-html " FILE"
.RB [ \-\-subject
.IR TEXT ]
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-cc
.IR LIST ]
.RB [ \-\-attach
.IR FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-text
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-require\-approval ]
.RB [ \-\-approve ]
.RB [ \-\-from\-mailbox
.IR ADDRESS ]
.RB [ \-\-save\-to\-sent
.IR BOOL ]
.br
.B mailer.py \-\-to\-operator
.BI \-\-message " TEXT"
.RB [ \-\-subject
.IR TEXT ]
.RB [ \-\-board\-id
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B mailer.py \-\-check
.RB [ \-\-from\-mailbox
.IR ADDRESS ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent mailer.py
.I options
.br
.B python3 $FLEET_CODE/lanes/mailer.py
.I options
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mailer.py
sends one message with Microsoft Graph
.BR sendMail ,
as the CTI mailbox, using the same Entra app registration the Go agent
reads that mailbox with (application permission
.BR Mail.Send ).
There are no SMTP credentials on the box. It is called by
.BR run\-digest (1)
for the daily and weekly digests and by
.BR run\-patchtuesday (1),
and by an operator by hand. The orchestrator heartbeat is deliberately not
allowed to run it; it escalates through
.BR cti\-alert (1).
Lanes never send mail.
.BR cti\-mailer (1)
is the Go port; the runners still call this one.
.PP
It sends either a rendered digest
.RB ( \-\-html )
or a short escalation
.RB ( \-\-message ),
exactly one of the two. An escalation is wrapped in plain HTML (paragraphs
split on blank lines) with instructions to reply keeping the
.BI "[FLEET " id ]
tag in the subject, so the orchestrator can match the reply back to the
board line.
.SS Recipients
.TP
.B To
With
.BR \-\-to\-operator :
.B FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL
alone. Otherwise
.BR \-\-to ,
else
.BR DIGEST_TO .
There is no built-in default; with neither, nothing is sent.
.TP
.B Cc
Never for
.BR \-\-to\-operator .
Otherwise
.BR \-\-cc ,
else
.BR DIGEST_CC ;
then, when
.B DIGEST_CC_FROM_ALLOW_TO
is true, every address in
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
as written (not the operator added below) that is not already there. Any
Cc address that is also a To address is dropped, compared without regard
to case.
.TP
.B Validation
Every address must look like
.IB local @ domain . tld
with no spaces.
.TP
.B Allowlist
The allowed set is
.BR FLEET_ALLOW_TO ,
or
.B DIGEST_TO
when that is unset, plus
.BR FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL ,
compared without regard to case. It covers To and Cc alike. Any recipient
outside it refuses the send unless
.B \-\-approve
is given. So the scheduled digest to
.B DIGEST_TO
and escalations to the operator pass, and anything else needs an explicit
approval for that one send.
.PP
The subject is
.B \-\-subject
or
.BR "CTI Brief YYYY\-MM\-DD" ,
local date. In
.B \-\-message
mode with
.BR \-\-board\-id ,
.BI "[FLEET " id "] "
is prepended unless already present. Whitespace is collapsed and the
subject cut to 255 characters. A subject starting
.B [Sev5]
is sent with high importance.
.PP
.I fleet.env
is read first, without overriding variables already in the environment;
lines are
.IB KEY = value\fR,
.B #
comments are skipped, and surrounding quotes are stripped.
.PP
A refusal is final: the message names the variable or flag to change.
Progress and errors go to standard error, prefixed
.BR [mailer] ;
the result goes to standard output as one JSON line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-html " FILE"
Send this rendered HTML file as the body. The file must exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-message " TEXT"
Send this short plain text, wrapped in minimal HTML. For escalations, not
digests.
.TP
.BI \-\-text " FILE"
Accepted for the plain-text alternative and ignored: Graph is sent one HTML
body, and the file is neither read nor checked.
.TP
.BI \-\-subject " TEXT"
The subject line.
Default:\~\fBCTI Brief\fR and today's date.
.TP
.BI \-\-to " LIST"
Comma-separated To addresses, replacing
.BR DIGEST_TO .
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-to\-operator .
.TP
.BI \-\-cc " LIST"
Comma-separated Cc addresses, replacing
.BR DIGEST_CC .
Subject to the allowlist like
.BR \-\-to .
Ignored with
.BR \-\-to\-operator .
.TP
.B \-\-to\-operator
Send to
.B FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL
only, with no Cc, whether the body is
.B \-\-message
or
.BR \-\-html . Pre-approved, because telling the operator something is
not an outward-facing send. Refused when that variable is unset.
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-mailbox " ADDRESS"
The mailbox to send as; the Graph path is
.BI /users/ ADDRESS /sendMail\fR.
Default:\~\fB$GRAPH_MAILBOX\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-attach " FILE"
Attach a file; repeat for more. A missing file, or one over 3,000,000
bytes, is skipped with a message and the send goes ahead. Files ending
.I .md
are sent as
.BR text/markdown ,
everything else as
.BR text/plain .
.TP
.BI \-\-board\-id " ID"
The board line id the escalation answers to, used in the
.BI "[FLEET " ID ]
subject tag and reply instructions.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Do everything except request a token and send: the recipient rules and
allowlist are applied, and a refusal is still a refusal. Prints
.B {"dry_run": true, ...}
with the mode, subject, To and Cc, and the HTML path, or in message mode
the rendered body.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-approval
Refuse unless
.B \-\-approve
is also given, whoever the recipients are. For off-cycle sends.
.TP
.B \-\-approve
The operator approved this specific send. Lifts the allowlist refusal and
satisfies
.BR \-\-require\-approval .
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-to\-sent " BOOL"
Keep a copy in the sending mailbox's Sent Items. Only
.B true
(any case) keeps it; any other value does not.
Default:\~\fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Preflight, then exit; every other option except
.B \-\-from\-mailbox
is ignored. Lists the
.I fleet.env
path, each required setting
.RB ( TENANT_ID ,
.BR CLIENT_ID ,
.BR CLIENT_SECRET ,
.BR GRAPH_MAILBOX ,
.BR FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL )
as
.B OK
or
.BR UNSET ,
and each optional one
.RB ( DIGEST_TO ,
.BR DIGEST_CC ,
.BR DIGEST_CC_FROM_ALLOW_TO ,
.BR FLEET_ALLOW_TO ,
.BR NVD_API_KEY ,
.BR CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN )
as
.B OK
or
.BR none .
If anything required is unset it stops there. Otherwise it requests a token
and decodes its granted application roles:
.B Mail.Read
or
.B Mail.ReadWrite
(read the mailbox) and
.B Mail.Send
are required and reported
.B MISSING
when absent;
.B Mail.ReadWrite
for mailbox cleanup is reported
.B absent
but is not a failure; and any role the code never calls is listed as
.B UNUSED
with a recommendation to remove it. Sends nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Read from the process environment after
.I fleet.env
is loaded (existing environment variables win). Sections refer to
.IR fleet.env .
.TP
.BR TENANT_ID ", " CLIENT_ID ", " CLIENT_SECRET
The Entra app registration, for the client-credentials token. Required to
send. Section 1, MICROSOFT GRAPH.
.TP
.B GRAPH_MAILBOX
Default for
.BR \-\-from\-mailbox ,
and the reply address named in an escalation. Section 1.
.TP
.B CTI_REPLY_MAILBOX
Overrides the reply address named in an escalation.
Default:\~\fB$GRAPH_MAILBOX\fR. Section 1.
.TP
.B DIGEST_TO
Default To list; the allowlist when
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
is unset. Section 4, RECIPIENTS AND THE SEND GATE.
.TP
.B DIGEST_CC
Default Cc list. Section 4.
.TP
.B DIGEST_CC_FROM_ALLOW_TO
.BR 1 ,
.BR true ,
.B yes
or
.B on
(any case) adds
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
to the Cc. Anything else is off. Section 4.
.TP
.B FLEET_ALLOW_TO
The recipient allowlist, comma-separated, covering To and Cc.
Default:\~\fB$DIGEST_TO\fR. Section 4.
.TP
.B FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL
Where
.B \-\-to\-operator
sends; always on the allowlist. Section 4.
.TP
.BR NVD_API_KEY ", " CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
Only reported by
.BR \-\-check .
Sections 6 and 7.
.TP
.B FLEET_ENV
Path of
.IR fleet.env .
Default:\~\fI$FLEET_HOME/fleet.env\fR; set to
.I /etc/cti\-agent/fleet.env
by the units and
.BR cti\-agent (1).
.TP
.B FLEET_HOME
Used only for the default
.BR FLEET_ENV .
Default:\~\fI~/fleet\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/fleet.env
Credentials and recipients;
.B root:ctiagent
0640.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/digest\-{daily,weekly}\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.html
The digests
.B run\-digest
passes as
.BR \-\-html .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Sent (Graph accepted it), or a dry run passed every check, or
.B \-\-check
found every required setting and role.
.TP
.B 1
Refused or failed: no sending mailbox; not exactly one of
.B \-\-html
and
.BR \-\-message ;
the HTML file is missing;
.B \-\-to\-operator
with
.B \-\-to
or with no
.BR FLEET_OPERATOR_EMAIL ;
no recipients; an invalid address; a recipient outside the allowlist
without
.BR \-\-approve ;
.B \-\-require\-approval
without
.BR \-\-approve ;
a token request that failed or a credential that is unset; Graph refused
the send (a 403 is explained as a missing
.B Mail.Send
permission, missing admin consent or an Application Access Policy; 429 and
503 are retried twice, honouring
.BR Retry\-After );
or
.B \-\-check
found a required setting unset or a required role missing.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option or a missing option value (argparse).
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the configuration and the token's permissions:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent mailer.py \-\-check
.EE
.PP
Validate today's digest against the gate without sending:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent mailer.py \-\-dry\-run \e
  \-\-html /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/digest\-daily\-$(date +%F).html
.EE
.PP
Escalate a question to the operator:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent mailer.py \-\-to\-operator \-\-board\-id q17 \e
  \-\-subject "Approve off\-cycle send?" \e
  \-\-message "CVE\-2026\-1234 is on KEV and present on 30 hosts."
.EE
.PP
A one-off send to someone not on the allowlist, after approval on the
board:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent mailer.py \-\-approve \-\-to someone@example.com \e
  \-\-html /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/digest\-daily\-$(date +%F).html
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-mailer (1),
.BR run\-digest (1),
.BR brief.py (1),
.BR fleet\-board (1),
.BR cti\-alert (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md sections 1 and 11b; fleet\-kit/README.md, "Recipients and the
send gate" and "Autonomy \- where the gates are".
